  "chapters": [
    {
      "id": "ch-1-niemen",
      "when": "1812-06-24",
      "dateLabel": {
        "en": "24 June 1812 (12 June Old Style)",
        "id": "24 Juni 1812 (12 Juni kalender Julian)"
      },
      "title": {
        "en": "Across the Niemen",
        "id": "Menyeberangi Neman"
      },
      "body": {
        "en": "On 24 June 1812 Napoleon's Grande Armée began crossing the Niemen into the Russian Empire. Charles Minard's famous map of 1869 counts 422,000 men; modern estimates for the first wave are a little higher.\n\nRussia still used the Julian calendar, twelve days behind. This dataset stores every date in the Gregorian calendar and shows the Old Style date as a label.",
        "id": "Pada 24 Juni 1812 Grande Armée pimpinan Napoleon mulai menyeberangi Sungai Neman memasuki wilayah Kekaisaran Rusia. Peta terkenal Charles Minard tahun 1869 mencatat 422.000 prajurit; perkiraan modern untuk gelombang pertama sedikit lebih tinggi.\n\nRusia masih memakai kalender Julian, dua belas hari lebih lambat. Dataset ini menyimpan semua tanggal dalam kalender Gregorian dan menampilkan tanggal kalender lama sebagai label."
      },
      "camera": {
        "center": [24.2, 54.9],
        "zoom": 8,
        "pitch": 40,
        "bearing": 60,
        "durationMs": 3000
      },
      "focus": ["niemen-crossing", "grande-armee-main", "grande-armee-north"],
      "media": ["minard-chart"],
      "sources": ["minard-1869", "wp-french-invasion"]
    },
    {
      "id": "ch-2-advance",
      "when": "1812-06-25/1812-08-15",
      "title": {
        "en": "The long advance",
        "id": "Gerak maju yang panjang"
      },
      "body": {
        "en": "The Russian armies fell back instead of giving battle. Napoleon entered Wilna on 28 June and Vitebsk at the end of July.\n\nWatch the line thin out. A northern flank turned off toward Polotsk, and by the time it reached Vitebsk the main body had lost half its strength to disease, desertion and detachments, before any major battle.",
        "id": "Tentara Rusia terus mundur alih-alih bertempur. Napoleon memasuki Wilna pada 28 Juni dan Vitebsk pada akhir Juli.\n\nPerhatikan garis pasukan yang makin menipis. Sayap utara berbelok ke arah Polotsk, dan saat tiba di Vitebsk, pasukan utama telah kehilangan separuh kekuatannya akibat penyakit, desersi, dan pemecahan pasukan, sebelum ada satu pun pertempuran besar."
      },
      "camera": {
        "center": [27.3, 55],
        "zoom": 6.3,
        "pitch": 30,
        "bearing": 0,
        "durationMs": 3000
      },
      "focus": ["grande-armee-main", "grande-armee-north", "vilnius-entered", "battle-of-vitebsk", "polotsk"],
      "sources": ["minard-1869", "napoleon-empire-daybyday"]
    },
    {
      "id": "ch-3-smolensk",
      "when": "1812-08-16/1812-09-06",
      "title": {
        "en": "Smolensk",
        "id": "Smolensk"
      },
      "body": {
        "en": "Napoleon stormed Smolensk on 16–18 August, but the Russian armies escaped east. Soon afterwards Mikhail Kutuzov took overall command of the Russian forces.",
        "id": "Napoleon menyerbu Smolensk pada 16–18 Agustus, tetapi tentara Rusia lolos ke timur. Tak lama kemudian Mikhail Kutuzov mengambil alih komando tertinggi pasukan Rusia."
      },
      "camera": {
        "center": [33, 55],
        "zoom": 7,
        "pitch": 35,
        "bearing": 20,
        "durationMs": 3000
      },
      "focus": ["battle-of-smolensk", "kutuzov-command", "grande-armee-main"],
      "sources": ["wp-smolensk", "wp-french-invasion"]
    },
    {
      "id": "ch-4-borodino",
      "when": "1812-09-07",
      "dateLabel": {
        "en": "7 September 1812 (26 August Old Style)",
        "id": "7 September 1812 (26 Agustus kalender Julian)"
      },
      "title": {
        "en": "Borodino",
        "id": "Borodino"
      },
      "body": {
        "en": "At Borodino, about 115 km west of Moscow, Kutuzov finally stood and fought. It was the bloodiest single day of the campaign, with some 30,000 to 42,000 French and 40,000 to 53,000 Russian casualties.\n\nKutuzov withdrew the next day, leaving the road to Moscow open.",
        "id": "Di Borodino, sekitar 115 km di barat Moskwa, Kutuzov akhirnya bertahan dan bertempur. Inilah hari paling berdarah dalam kampanye ini, dengan korban sekitar 30.000 hingga 42.000 di pihak Prancis dan 40.000 hingga 53.000 di pihak Rusia.\n\nKutuzov mundur keesokan harinya, membiarkan jalan ke Moskwa terbuka."
      },
      "camera": {
        "center": [35.817, 55.533],
        "zoom": 11,
        "pitch": 55,
        "bearing": 80,
        "durationMs": 3500
      },
      "focus": ["battle-of-borodino", "borodino"],
      "sources": ["wp-borodino"]
    },
    {
      "id": "ch-5-moscow",
      "when": "1812-09-08/1812-10-18",
      "title": {
        "en": "Moscow burns",
        "id": "Moskwa terbakar"
      },
      "body": {
        "en": "The French entered an almost empty Moscow on 14 September. That night fires broke out, and by 18 September about three quarters of the city had burned.\n\nNapoleon waited five weeks for a peace offer that never came.",
        "id": "Pasukan Prancis memasuki Moskwa yang nyaris kosong pada 14 September. Malam itu kebakaran terjadi, dan hingga 18 September sekitar tiga perempat kota telah hangus.\n\nNapoleon menunggu lima minggu untuk tawaran damai yang tak pernah datang."
      },
      "camera": {
        "center": [37.62, 55.75],
        "zoom": 10.5,
        "pitch": 45,
        "bearing": -20,
        "durationMs": 3500
      },
      "focus": ["moscow-entered", "fire-of-moscow", "moscow"],
      "sources": ["wp-fire-of-moscow"]
    },
    {
      "id": "ch-6-retreat",
      "when": "1812-10-19/1812-11-09",
      "title": {
        "en": "The retreat begins",
        "id": "Mundur dimulai"
      },
      "body": {
        "en": "About 108,000 men left Moscow on 19 October, heading south-west. At Maloyaroslavets on 24 October the Russians blocked the way, forcing the army back onto the road it had already stripped bare on the way in.\n\nAfter another defeat at Vyazma on 3 November, the first hard frosts arrived.",
        "id": "Sekitar 108.000 prajurit meninggalkan Moskwa pada 19 Oktober menuju barat daya. Di Maloyaroslavets pada 24 Oktober pasukan Rusia menutup jalan, memaksa mereka kembali ke jalan yang sudah mereka jarah habis saat berangkat.\n\nSetelah kalah lagi di Vyazma pada 3 November, embun beku pertama yang keras pun datang."
      },
      "camera": {
        "center": [35.9, 55.3],
        "zoom": 7.3,
        "pitch": 35,
        "bearing": 0,
        "durationMs": 3500
      },
      "focus": ["moscow-departure", "battle-of-maloyaroslavets", "battle-of-vyazma", "grande-armee-main"],
      "sources": ["wp-fire-of-moscow", "wp-maloyaroslavets", "wp-vyazma"]
    },
    {
      "id": "ch-7-krasnoi",
      "when": "1812-11-10/1812-11-25",
      "title": {
        "en": "Smolensk and Krasnoi",
        "id": "Smolensk dan Krasnoi"
      },
      "body": {
        "en": "Minard recorded −21° Réaumur (about −26 °C) on 14 November.\n\nAt Krasnoi, on 15–18 November, the Russians took about 26,500 prisoners.",
        "id": "Minard mencatat suhu −21° Réaumur (sekitar −26 °C) pada 14 November.\n\nDi Krasnoi, pada 15–18 November, pasukan Rusia menawan sekitar 26.500 prajurit."
      },
      "camera": {
        "center": [31.4, 54.6],
        "zoom": 7.8,
        "pitch": 35,
        "bearing": 0,
        "durationMs": 3000
      },
      "focus": ["battle-of-krasnoi", "grande-armee-main"],
      "sources": ["wp-krasnoi", "minard-1869"]
    },
    {
      "id": "ch-8-berezina",
      "when": "1812-11-26/1812-12-04",
      "title": {
        "en": "The Berezina",
        "id": "Berezina"
      },
      "body": {
        "en": "Trapped between two Russian armies at the Berezina, Napoleon's engineers built two trestle bridges at Studienka. The remnant crossed between 26 and 29 November, and the northern flank rejoined it there. Between 50,000 and 60,000 were lost.",
        "id": "Terjepit di antara dua tentara Rusia di Sungai Berezina, para zeni Napoleon membangun dua jembatan darurat di Studienka. Sisa pasukan menyeberang antara 26 dan 29 November, dan sayap utara bergabung kembali di sana. Antara 50.000 dan 60.000 orang hilang."
      },
      "camera": {
        "center": [28.4, 54.28],
        "zoom": 9.5,
        "pitch": 50,
        "bearing": -30,
        "durationMs": 3500
      },
      "focus": ["battle-of-berezina", "grande-armee-main", "grande-armee-north"],
      "sources": ["wp-berezina", "minard-1869"]
    },
    {
      "id": "ch-9-niemen-again",
      "when": "1812-12-05/1812-12-14",
      "title": {
        "en": "Back across the Niemen",
        "id": "Kembali menyeberangi Neman"
      },
      "body": {
        "en": "On 5 December at Smorgoni Napoleon left the army for Paris. Minard's temperatures fell to −30° Réaumur.\n\nIn mid-December the survivors recrossed the Niemen. Of the 422,000 men in Minard's count, about 10,000 came back.",
        "id": "Pada 5 Desember di Smorgoni, Napoleon meninggalkan pasukannya menuju Paris. Suhu dalam catatan Minard turun hingga −30° Réaumur.\n\nPada pertengahan Desember para penyintas menyeberangi Neman kembali. Dari 422.000 prajurit dalam hitungan Minard, sekitar 10.000 yang kembali."
      },
      "camera": {
        "center": [25.2, 54.5],
        "zoom": 7.2,
        "pitch": 30,
        "bearing": 0,
        "durationMs": 3500
      },
      "focus": ["napoleon-leaves", "niemen-recrossed", "grande-armee-main"],
      "media": ["minard-chart"],
      "sources": ["minard-1869", "masswerk-minard", "napoleon-empire-daybyday"]
    }
  ],
